      "worked": "Let $x=P(A)$, so $P(B)=2x$. Independence gives $P(A\\cap B)=x(2x)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A\\cup B)&=x+2x-x(2x)\\\\P(A\\cup B)&=3x-2x^2\\\\0.72&=3x-2x^2\\\\2x^2-3x+0.72&=0\\\\(x-0.3)(x-1.2)&=0\\\\x&=0.3\\text{ or }1.2.\\end{align*}$$\nThe value $1.2$ cannot be a probability. Therefore, $P(A)=0.3$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
